WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.400
Eek!

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.400
Somebody help!

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.600
Are you... a hero?

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.570
So this... is a battle...

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.350
But in order to return to my own world,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.580
I have no choice but to fight!

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.590
I came here 'cause the
white girl told me so.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:08.020
Are you Yuusuke Yotsuya?

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:10.780
How does she know my name?

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.170
I will judge you.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.860
That's what the white girl told me to do.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.850
White girl? Wait, you mean...

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:23.030
One of the people you will meet in
the near future will be the sixth.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:29.620
I'm Glenda, 'cause I take videos of you.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.590
Is she the sixth?

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:39.660
I'm a videographer, you see.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.700
Okay, but...

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.300
Why did she come to my grandpa's house?

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.910
I'm traveling the world to
make an independent film.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:48.790
Um...

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:49.770
Yes?

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.780
So... Glenda-san...

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.050
You can call me Glen.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:56.220
Glen-san, have you been to the
other world several times?

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:58.660
No, I've never been there.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.230
Huh? Then...

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:05.520
I guess sometimes the Game Master shows
up before we're transported there?

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:10.080
It's probably because I
already knew about you guys.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.200
You did?

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:16.380
I know four people online who insist
they've been to another world and back.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:17.600
Four?!

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:18.710
Which means...

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.550
Everyone but me?

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.950
One's American, one's French,

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:27.130
one's Egyptian, and one's Japanese.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.000
Huh?

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.560
They've each described a world
that's perfectly identical

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.700
to what the other three describe,
down to the smallest detail.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:38.130
Of course, none of them have
any other sort of connection.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.860
That must mean the Master
appeared to them, too...

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.570
And it's not just the five of us?

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:48.240
The Japanese person's username is Yukarion.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.370
Ring any bells?

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.410
That's her.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:57.340
I liked this French woman.
Her looks were just my type.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.250
Your type?

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.400
I'm only interested in women.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.040
Huh?

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.000
Did she just casually come out?

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.630
But sadly, she passed away.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:08.630
Huh?

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.000
Heart failure, apparently.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:14.200
The last comment she left said,
"Cleared the fourth round.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.680
Now the fifth round is about to start."

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.190
She failed a quest?!

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:23.100
Is there any way to contact these people?

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.100
I tried it,

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.910
by posting comments on each of their videos.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.070
Of course.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.040
But none of them have replied.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:37.590
I don't know if they missed my
comments or just ignored them,

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:38.890
or perhaps...

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.620
They failed?

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:46.050
So why don't we start
posting stuff ourselves?

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.030
Posting?

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.210
Remember what I said before?

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.050
Let me take videos of you.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:00.180
We have such cute visitors!

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.480
U-Um... My name is... uh...

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:04.820
Uh... I'm... Shindou!

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.510
Yo, Yuusuke, who are these two?

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.310
Your g-girlfriend?

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.560
Which one, though?

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.760
Surely not both of them, right?

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.390
The actors have come together!

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.660
Naw, they're just classmates.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.810
She's the real deal.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:25.420
I just brought 'em out 'cause
we need 'em for our video.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.440
Wow...

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:26.950
Huh?

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:30.710
So you speak in the local dialect
when you're back home, huh?

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:34.530
What difference does that make?

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.510
Hi.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:37.780
Uh...

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.590
Hi...

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:40.360
H-Hello.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.680
Anyway, that script I emailed you...

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:43.840
I read it.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.630
You came up with a pretty good
reproduction of our adventures.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.590
We don't have much time or funding,

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:52.170
but she says she'll take
care of everything else.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.860
Huh...

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:57.070
I dunno if it's 'cause they're here or what,

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.970
but did ya suddenly lose yer accent?

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:00.220
Totally!

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.450
This is killing me...

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.760
Glen's suggestion was...

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:13.950
Well, I guess we don't <i>not</i> look like a warrior
and a citizen of another world... maybe?

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:17.790
Yeah... I mean... sort of.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:19.700
Action!

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:23.050
What is this place?! Who are you?!

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.980
...that we make a short
film of our experiences

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.570
and upload it to the internet.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.580
Game Master at your serv.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.630
I will now explain the rules to.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.610
G-Game? Rules?

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:41.970
What do you mean?

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:48.470
But we have to present it in a way that
other players would recognize instantly.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.550
Eek!

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:52.390
Somebody help!

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.630
Are you... a hero?

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:56.980
A hero?

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:01.600
Oh, I get it. I'm known
as a hero in this world!

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.660
I have to defeat these guys,

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:08.280
or I can't complete the quest I was given!

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.330
So this... is a battle...

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:19.000
But in order to return to my own world,

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.290
I have no choice but to fight!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.830
Considering the number of
views this stuff gets,

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:28.330
there's a good chance some players
will be among its viewers.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:29.330
Okay!

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:33.360
That was great, Iu-chan! You were so cool!

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:38.020
I guess we made it work.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.070
Long day, huh?

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.840
Thanks for coming all the way out here.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.700
I had nothing else to do,
and it was pretty fun.

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:50.060
So about my pay...

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:50.620
Huh?!

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:53.590
I <i>am</i> an amateur model, you know.

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.160
How could you not pay me?

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.660
W-We talked about this, remember?

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.650
We're doing this for our own benefit!

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:03.630
Okay, then, just do one thing I ask,
and I'll let you off the hook.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:06.320
Huh? Yeah, sure, that's fine.

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.250
No being polite.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.020
Huh?

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:13.420
When you're here, you're not just
speaking in your local dialect.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.290
You're different in every way.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:19.150
I want you to be like that around us, too.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:23.970
And that concludes this business discussion!

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.680
Damn it!

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:29.290
A few days later,
our short film was completed

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:31.520
and uploaded to a video site.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:34.450
Then, ten days after its release...

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:43.440
The occupation of the sixth
player, Glenda Carter, is...

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:48.330
Warrior (Axe).

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.840
A fourth Warrior, huh?

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:58.420
But I use a spear, Iu-chan uses a sword,

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:00.770
and Kusue-chan's a... huh?

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.650
A Heavy Warrior?!

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:06.060
That's an elite job.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.270
Kusue, when did that happen?

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:11.060
Oh, uh... on Jiffon Island...

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.770
When the Orc Queen died.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:21.330
Hakozaki Kusue: Heavy Warrior (Sword).

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:24.560
I put the armor back since
it's heavy, though.

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:30.160
So even with all these Warriors,
there are no duplicates.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.640
Her stats are definitely high.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.080
Maybe she'll finally be strong
enough to keep up with us now?

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:40.230
Now, your quest for the
fifth round is as fol.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:46.890
A: Reduce Rainbow Stair addiction in
the Kingdom of Goldia to less than 3%.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.780
The time limit is 90 days.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.010
B: Stop the destruction of
the village of Zagroth.

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:55.380
The time limit is 30 days.

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:56.720
Huh?

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.640
What... the heck?

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:02.970
You may choose whichever one you pref.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:07.110
Oh, man! We have two options this time?

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:09.730
B sounds like it'd be easier.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:11.920
It requires a lot less time, too.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:15.750
No, wait... The simpler a quest sounds,

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.860
the more ambiguous its goal is.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:23.270
With stuff like this, we tend to lose a lot
of time just figuring out what we need to do.

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.650
We should choose A.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:27.190
All right, A—

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:27.440
Okay, we'll take B.

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:27.710
Huh?

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:29.100
Underst.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:32.570
Excuse me?! Who said you could decide?!

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.620
Bye.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:35.620
Wait—

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:36.970
You dick!

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:39.840
What's the problem?
B's easier to make sense of.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.290
It'll take less time, too.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:43.370
That's exactly what the problem is!

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:45.200
Well, the decision's made now.
We can't change it.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.810
Why?!

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:48.780
I guess we need to find the
village of Zagroth first.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.540
Should we go to Cortonel
and ask Kahvel-san again?

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:00.130
How many years has it been since last time?

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:03.710
Damn... It looks totally different.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:07.270
Hey, where was Kahvel-san's house again?

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:10.150
If I recall, it should be over there.

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:12.060
Too polite. Try again.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:16.480
I-I think it was over there?

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:23.190
Kahvel-san!

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:41.290
Thank you for all you did for
my mother when she was alive.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.480
You really haven't changed at all.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:52.350
They won't go all the way to the village,

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:55.600
but these merchants will give
you a ride partway there.

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:57.700
Thanks for everything.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:02.520
Traveling with you heroes was my
mother's proudest accomplishment.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.490
I heard the stories of
her adventures with you

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:11.170
as bedtime stories from a very young age.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:14.020
If I can be of any help to you at all,

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:16.800
I'm sure it will make her very happy.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:31.490
That little girl is already...

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:34.300
It's been seventeen years.

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:36.200
It makes sense she'd grow up.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:38.980
I suddenly feel super old.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:44.990
So a lot of time passes in this
world with every round we complete?

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:48.910
Yeah. It's the one thing I
still can't get used to.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:58.900
Traveling with you heroes was my
mother's proudest accomplishment.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:01.470
Her proudest...

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:02.440
What?

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:03.380
Nothing.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:08.080
Wasn't I just using her?

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.970
So I could keep myself alive?

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:17.030
And from now on, I'll probably still...

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:24.790
Damn it!

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:26.810
How is there not even a road there?

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.240
Why do we have to walk
through all this crap?

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.160
This seriously sucks.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.270
A cart definitely couldn't
drive through this.

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:36.950
The sun is going down.

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:39.950
At the very least, we need
to find some kind of hint,

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:43.640
or we could end up lost
in this jungle forever.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:44.580
Y—

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:45.510
You're joking!

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:48.430
We should be going in the right direction...

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:54.820
Kahvel-san's daughter said Zagroth
doesn't get a lot of traffic,

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:56.770
but the location is so unclear.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:14:00.200
Forget villages. There aren't
even any signs of human life.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:03.860
Anyway, Glen-san,
your Japanese is really good.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.430
Where'd you learn it?

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:05.990
Huh?

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:09.810
Now that you mention it, you were
speaking English back in our world.

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:12.100
No, I'm speaking in English now.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:15.130
No way. All I hear is Japanese.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:17.730
It sounds like English to me.

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:20.170
So does what you're saying, Yukarion.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:24.330
Um... Could you not call me that, please?

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:27.540
I think our voices are being
automatically translated.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:29.070
Wait, you knew?!

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:31.000
It just took you too long to notice.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:35.990
I thought it was normal just because
of the kind of world this is...

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:38.290
What's that?

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:40.470
A goblin!

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:45.150
Not a human to be found,
but these guys are here?

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.860
You guys just stay put.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:54.250
Hey, Yuusuke! How the hell did you
change jobs on the way here?!

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:55.960
Huh? Oh...

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.800
I'll beat up the small fry myself!

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.290
Experience hog. So cheap.

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:03.200
Go for it.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:16.380
Shit!

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:21.480
Damn it!

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:30.890
Wind!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.540
It didn't even unbalance him?

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.910
This is just a regular goblin, right?

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.410
The weak things?

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:43.330
I-It should be...

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:47.540
It's coming this way!

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:50.680
W-Well, I've gotten stronger, too!

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.680
I see. So that's how it works.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.530
We don't really have any place here, do we?

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:00.600
Nope...

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:04.200
Down in one hit. Sad.

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:07.670
Hang on, were goblins always that strong?

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:09.440
Yeah, good point...

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:13.860
If it was red all over,
it might make sense, but...

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.610
That's pretty common in games.

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:17.580
Threat level D?!

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:19.660
What is it?

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:23.370
I took a look at this guy's
abilities with my Chef skill.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:24.740
Something strange?

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:25.700
Yes.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:31.840
Usually, the threat level of this type
of goblin would be F, the lowest rank,

00:16:32.230 --> 00:16:34.770
but this goblin's threat level is D.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:37.340
I've never seen this before.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.420
I saw someone.

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:40.160
Really?

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:40.920
Yeah.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:43.930
Glen-san!

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:45.680
We'll go, too.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.370
Is this a graveyard?

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:59.130
It's very old.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:02.290
Glen-san.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:04.170
Where are the others?

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:06.170
We split up to search.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.470
Did you lose sight of them?

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:09.870
No, I think...

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:25.900
Found her.

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:28.780
It looks like... she's scared.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:30.310
She's just a child.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:34.220
A huge woman like me would
only scare her more.

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:35.750
I'll let you handle it.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:37.220
H-Huh?!

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:44.820
I-It's okay. We won't do anything to you.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.140
We'd like to talk to you, if you don't mind.

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:50.170
Great... Hero?

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:50.710
Huh?

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.550
Yeah, that's right! You know about us?

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:56.700
That's right. We're heroes.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:18:00.110
So you don't need to worry.

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:12.440
My name is Jezby.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:16.230
So... Jezby, why did you run away from us?

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:19.620
I'm sorry. I thought you
were from the village.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:20.670
Village?

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:23.320
Are you from the village of Zagroth?

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.430
We're trying to get to Zagroth.

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:29.090
Where is the village?

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:37.340
A mountain?

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:40.180
No, that's a monolith.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:40.850
A what?

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.000
It's also called a volcanic plug.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:45.360
They're created when magma
from underground cools

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:47.210
and hardens above the surface.

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:50.780
There's a famous one in Wyoming
called Devil's Tower.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:52.340
I've heard of that.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:54.430
That's where the village is.

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:56.800
What? We have to climb that?

00:18:56.800 --> 00:19:00.700
Is that even possible without some
kind of winged monster to ride?

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:04.770
Now I see why they have little
interaction with the outside world.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:08.450
But this girl is on the outside now.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.640
Could you show us the way to that village?

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:15.690
No, she can't do that.

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:16.470
Huh?

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:20.640
She ran from us because she thought
we were from the village.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:25.600
They're chasing her?

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.520
I get my water from there.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.050
There are edible fruits
in the trees up ahead.

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:37.210
I'll go get some.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.810
I'll go with you, then.

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:41.790
That's all right. I do this every day.

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:44.150
You can go back to the hut and wait for me.

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:46.170
That's cold!

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:50.480
If this wasn't a quest,
it'd be kind of fun, like camping.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:51.910
What's the matter?

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:59.410
Oh, I was thinking it must be rough for
a child like her to survive alone.

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:03.670
Glen-san, do you not like children?

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:05.560
No, I like them.

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:07.790
And when we're talking about
a cute girl like her,

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:10.990
I'd probably like her even
more once she turned 18.

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:12.330
Once she's 18?

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:15.470
I'm just saying she's not
the right age for me yet.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:20.080
I'm only interested in women.

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.780
Huh?! Y-You mean...

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:24.710
Don't worry.

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:28.690
Even men don't go after every
single woman they meet, right?

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:31.700
Oh... You're right. I'm sorry.

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:34.360
I've just never known anyone like that...

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:37.610
I really am sorry.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:40.780
Don't worry about it.

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:43.310
You look cute that way, too.

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:50.690
My heart actually started
racing for a second...

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.510
Jezby-chan?

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:58.440
Wow...

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.700
Creature magic's pretty handy, huh?

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:01.350
Yeah.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:05.120
This is definitely using
less MP than it used to.

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:09.710
Well, that just means I can
make these plants grow faster.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:11.670
That's good, right?

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:13.510
Stop staring and help me out!

00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:14.620
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.040
We got firewood.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.840
Hey, welcome back.

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:21.450
Why are we doing the physical labor?

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:23.290
Well, you're a Hunter now, remember?

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:25.060
This is your chance to show off your skills.

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:31.300
Is this a monster?

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:32.310
Or is it...

00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:34.740
I... I don't know...

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:38.000
Father?

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.470
Next week on <i>Million Lives</i>...

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:29.580
"Tokitate Falls in Love through the Suspension
Bridge Effect!? ~Crash Landing of Passion~,"

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:30.980
"Yotsuya Versus Mecha Yotsuya,"

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:33.710
and "Glenda Super Chats
a Vtuber," three altogeth.

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:35.500
Don't miss next week's episo!

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:37.560
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:23:38.010 --> 00:23:39.900
I have cut another unworthy—
